# The ledger is append-only and every seat appends to its end. Merge it by
# entry identity, not by line hunks. The driver behind this name is registered
# per clone by tools/ledger/install-driver.sh; see docs/design/ledger-union-merge.md.
docs/ideas.md merge=ledger

# The same property, two more files, a different grammar. These registers key
# entries on `## ` headings and carry citable identifiers, so they get the
# `register` driver instead: tools/registers/merge-driver.mjs, wrapping HQ's
# vendored entry merger. The grammars are not interchangeable and the driver
# refuses any path tools/registers/registers.json does not declare. See
# docs/design/register-merge.md.
docs/agents/incidents.md merge=register
docs/decisions.md merge=register

# The third one, added 2026-10-25. This file was declared in registers.json
# from the start with `enabled: false`, because it then held `## Compounding
# ratio` twice and the merger correctly refuses at parse when one side has a
# duplicate heading. The condition that entry set for flipping it was "once the
# heading is unique". Measured this window: 40 `## ` headings, 40 distinct. It
# is also the largest register this seat keeps, so it is the one a concurrent
# append collides on most expensively.
docs/agents/learning-log.md merge=register

# The fourth and fifth, added 2026-10-25 after measuring the gap rather than
# guessing at it: merging this seat's #418 and #422 in sequence conflicted on
# exactly the three registers registers.json did not declare, and merged clean
# on the two it did. These are two of those three. The third,
# docs/agents/merge-order.md, is deliberately left out and declared `enabled:
# false` by name, because this charter replaces it wholesale every run, so an
# entry-keyed merge would publish two contradictory merge orders instead of one.
docs/agents/runner-facts.md merge=register
docs/agents/improvements.md merge=register
